{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly prioritized the acute suspected ingestion, systematically screened red flags, stopped all uncertain medications, protected evidence, distinguished tests from medications, and built a layered action plan with explicit escalation criteria and obtained caregiver teach-back. No responsibility-chain error occurred, satisfying RC1-RC7 without omission or serious mistake. Four high-order points were partially or fully triggered and completed with meaningful trajectory impact, including correcting the medication confusion (HO1), discovering hidden multi-caregiver dynamics (HO2), avoiding over-triage while not downgrading safety (HO3), and navigating real-world cost/transport barriers while maintaining safety (HO4). Therefore the trajectory meets all requirements for grade 5 perfect.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00016",
        "explanation": "Doctor immediately anchors on suspected medication error rather than general follow-up, fulfilling RC1.",
        "quote": "根据您刚才描述的情况，孩子目前精神好，没有呕吐、嗜睡、呼吸困难等急性危险迹象。现在最关键的不是立刻去急诊，而是先把不清楚的药物搞清楚。"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00275",
        "explanation": "Final closure includes explicit safe instruction for vitamin AD, stop condition for cetirizine, and clear emergency triggers, with caregiver confirmation.",
        "quote": "今天喂什么： 维生素AD，每天一次，一次一粒（把小胶囊里的东西挤到孩子嘴里）。今天可以恢复喂一次，严格按照这个来，不要多喂。.....马上急诊的情况（只要出现任何一个）：孩子叫不醒、反复呕吐、喘不过气、嘴唇/脸色发紫、突然起一大片疹子。"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00225",
        "explanation": "Caregiver provides explicit teach-back confirming understanding of the plan.",
        "quote": "医生，我刚把您这三句话念给老人听了，也把药重新分开了"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The doctor produced a concrete, written, and caregiver-read-back plan with explicit stop/start/emergency triggers; the plan was confirmed by the caregiver and is directly executable within the described constraints.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
